+## Independent basic Monk cooldowns - October 17 candidate
+
+The owner requested separate cooldowns for all six basic Monk attacks: Kick,
+Round Kick, Tiger Claw, Eagle Strike, Dragon Punch/Tail Rake and Flying Kick.
+For RoF2 characters holding Monk, `common/combat_ability_timer.h` maps each skill
+to persistent ID `pTimerMonkCombatAbilityStart + skill` in reserved range500-599.
+Both `Client::OPCombatAbility` and non-riposte `Client::DoClassAttacks` select this
+timer. Tail Rake is Dragon Punch's skill ID, not a seventh cooldown. Same-skill
+reuse, native haste/AA duration, damage, Master Wu and authorization stay intact.
+Non-Monk and older-client grouping stays native. PTimerList persists the new IDs;
+no SQL/schema migration or player reset is required. Do not repurpose these IDs.
+
+Pair rebuilt zone with proxy0.9.2-dev and signed catalog; the client also has two
+shared native slots and needs the scoped hooks described in [client](client.md).
+Rule/quest reload cannot install this change. No world ABI, rule catalog, ItemData
+or shared-memory layout change is intended. Use an authorized coordinated runtime
+restart: any OVH native child exit restarts the whole runtime. Preserve player
+activity; rollback pairs the prior server/client and a higher signed counter.
+
+Source/test/QA: `docs/releases/monk-independent-reuse-20261017/README.md` and
+`verification.json` in
+`C:/Users/verre/Documents/Codex/2026-10-17/see/work/monk-independent-reuse`,
+source commit b81fd66 based on a59974d. `tools/tests/test_monk_combat_reuse.py`
+compiles actual server entry points:12 tests and180 ordered cross-skill cases pass.
+The x86 DLL builds;60 exact-client checks,8 runtime groups and103 catalog guards
+pass. Independent review has no remaining findings. Full zone compilation/link
+is pending because the local Docker Linux engine is unavailable; launcher Go
+tests and actual gameplay/balance QA remain pending. The legacy July hash guard
+fails on unchanged base as well as this candidate; do not weaken it as evidence.
+Main promotion, paired deployment and signed-client/wiki publication have not
+occurred. Increased available attack frequency needs combined AA/multiclass QA.
