+## Independent Monk reuse - October 17 candidate
+
+Proxy0.9.2-dev adds six per-skill start/duration/readiness records in
+`eq-client-dll/src/monk_reuse.h`, scoped to current matched identity holding Monk.
+Six guarded SkillManager methods keep native duration adjustment and expiration
+callbacks. The shared native special-attack entry at RVA0x1A5000 exchanges only
+the selected EQPlayer shared slot and restores it in `__finally`, including on
+failure. This entry covers hotbuttons and native ability controls; a hotbutton-only
+scope misses other activation routes. The later stock commit at RVA0x5D96C must
+retain the captured independent timestamp instead of the restored shared value.
+Missing/stale identity and other skills forward to native trampolines.
+
+`ui_hooks.h::StateHook` clears transient records when leaving game state5;
+persistent server timers still enforce reuse through zone/relog. `dllmain.cpp`
+installs the hooks behind the existing monk_attacks required feature. Exact
+signatures and version are generated from patch-sites.json and its verifier;
+proxy and launcher catalogs must agree. The pinned eqgame.exe is read-only.
+
+Pair with the server mapping in [multiclass](multiclass.md). Both sides must ship
+together; this candidate is not published or installed. Native source fixture
+`tests/monk-reuse-native.cpp` reproduces10 failures before repair and now passes60
+checks, including the installed submitter/stock commit and exception cleanup.
+Targeting/damage/time remain controlled fixture boundaries. Full x86 DLL and20
+test executables build;8 runtime groups and103 exact guards pass. Full zone build,
+launcher Go tests, live countdown/combat/balance QA and release approval remain
+pending. Evidence and seven-step owner QA:
+`docs/releases/monk-independent-reuse-20261017/` in the October17 Monk checkout
+listed in multiclass.md; reviewed source b81fd66. Preserve all current managed
+assets/history at publication and use a fresh signed channel counter.
